WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.456
This lesson shows you how to create an approved blog post or update an existing one.

2
00:00:05.456 --> 00:00:18.089
We will keep new work in Draft, complete the article, category, featured image, links, and search information, preview everything, save once, clear the applicable cache, and verify the public article.

3
00:00:18.089 --> 00:00:20.616
No test post is created for this lesson.

4
00:00:20.966 --> 00:00:26.203
You need an Editor or Administrator account. Editor access is enough for blog posts.

5
00:00:26.203 --> 00:00:29.009
Do not use Administrator for routine writing.

6
00:00:29.009 --> 00:00:37.802
If Posts is missing from the left menu, stop and ask the website administrator instead of changing your role or using another person's login.

7
00:00:38.152 --> 00:00:48.682
Before opening Posts, gather the final approved title and article copy, the approved existing category, the featured image with permission to use it, and every link.

8
00:00:48.682 --> 00:00:54.553
Do not invent health claims, prices, dates, author details, image rights, or search wording.

9
00:00:54.903 --> 00:00:59.116
Open Posts. Use Add New Post only for an approved new article.

10
00:00:59.116 --> 00:01:04.688
For an update, open All Posts, match the exact title and author, then select Edit.

11
00:01:04.688 --> 00:01:12.299
Never overwrite another article because its title looks similar. Keep every new article in Draft while you work.

12
00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:17.842
Enter the approved title exactly. Add the complete article in the main Visual editor.

13
00:01:17.842 --> 00:01:23.339
Use clear headings, short paragraphs, and lists when they make the article easier to read.

14
00:01:23.339 --> 00:01:29.570
Select Save Draft while working. Do not publish an article that is incomplete or waiting for approval.

15
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.901
Open Categories and select the one approved category that best fits the article.

16
00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:42.061
Do not create a new category or guess. Use tags only when the approved website process specifically calls for them.

17
00:01:42.061 --> 00:01:45.921
Too many categories and tags make the Blog harder to organize.

18
00:01:46.271 --> 00:01:53.378
Choose an approved landscape image that belongs to the article. Confirm that it is clear and cropped correctly.

19
00:01:53.378 --> 00:01:58.243
Add useful alt text that describes the image's important subject or purpose.

20
00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:05.542
Do not use copyrighted, private, blurry, stretched, or unrelated imagery, and do not stuff keywords into alt text.

21
00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:12.369
Select descriptive words in the article and use the Link control. Paste the exact destination address.

22
00:02:12.369 --> 00:02:16.624
Add relevant internal links to Rebekah's pages or related articles.

23
00:02:16.624 --> 00:02:22.593
Use a new tab for an external link only when appropriate. Preview and test every changed link.

24
00:02:22.943 --> 00:02:30.371
In the S E O Press section, use the approved search title and a clear description that accurately summarizes the article.

25
00:02:30.371 --> 00:02:33.748
Keep the wording natural and inside the preview length.

26
00:02:33.748 --> 00:02:38.230
Do not repeat locations, services, or keywords simply to fill the fields.

27
00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:45.757
Select Preview. Check the title, headings, paragraphs, category, image, alt text, author, and links.

28
00:02:45.757 --> 00:02:48.986
Repeat the preview at desktop and phone size.

29
00:02:48.986 --> 00:02:55.876
If anything is wrong or uncertain, return to the editor, correct it, and keep the post in Draft.

30
00:02:56.226 --> 00:02:59.959
Use Publish only when a new article is complete and approved.

31
00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:03.447
Use Update for an approved change to an existing article.

32
00:03:03.447 --> 00:03:07.915
Select the correct button one time, then wait for WordPress confirmation.

33
00:03:07.915 --> 00:03:12.872
Do not click repeatedly and do not create a duplicate post to fix a saving delay.

34
00:03:13.222 --> 00:03:20.900
Clear only the applicable post or approved page cache. Open the exact public article address with no extra text.

35
00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:26.658
Verify the visible article, image, category, and links, then check the Blog archive.

36
00:03:26.658 --> 00:03:30.154
Repeat the public check at desktop and phone sizes.

37
00:03:30.504 --> 00:03:33.533
Every blog change ends with the same sequence.

38
00:03:33.533 --> 00:03:44.990
Keep new work in Draft, preview carefully, publish or update once, clear only the applicable cache, and verify the exact public article and Blog archive on desktop and phone.

39
00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.480
If anything is uncertain, stop and contact Blue Nova.
